{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache_interface", "label": "Cache interface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seven operations (get, set, incr, setIfAbsent, delete, mget, mset) cover about 95% of real cases; deliberately no pattern scans and no pub/sub, since the cluster has its own."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_opportunistic_semantics", "label": "Opportunistic, lossy-by-design cache semantics", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A None means \"not cached\" and the caller falls back to the source of truth; implementations return defaults on transient failures rather than throwing, and only misuse throws."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_set_if_absent", "label": "setIfAbsent atomic compare-and-set", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Atomicity is a guarantee, not best effort: every backend maps it onto a single native compare-and-set (Redis SET NX, Memcached ADD, an uninterleavable Map read/write pair in-process). No backend implements it as get-then-set, which would let two callers both observe the key absent. ttlMs applies only to the winning write, so a retry loop cannot extend someone else's hold."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_acquire_lock", "label": "acquireLock token-guarded lock", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Writes a random 128-bit token and deletes the key only if that token is still there; the naive delete-in-finally evicts the new owner once a holder overruns its TTL. ttlMs is required because expiry is the recovery path from a crashed holder. Not a consensus lock: the compare-and-delete is a get then a delete, not one atomic step, so guard with a fencing token where two holders would be a correctness bug."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_atomic_increment", "label": "Atomic increment (incr)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns the new count; the TTL is applied only when the counter is created, which is the right semantics for a fixed-window rate limiter."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_bulk_operations", "label": "Bulk cache operations (mget / mset)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Round-trip optimisation, critical for shared-entity hydration after a sharding rebalance: one call instead of N."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_opportunistic_semantics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_set_if_absent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_atomic_increment", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_bulk_operations", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_acquire_lock", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_set_if_absent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_inmemorycache", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_memcachedcache", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_acquire_lock", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_guarantee_carrying_entries", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_one_cache_per_consumer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_fi